1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:04,671
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:12,595
<i>Emilia had him killed.</i>

3
00:00:12,679 --> 00:00:14,472
<i>I'll kill her!</i>

4
00:00:14,556 --> 00:00:15,598
[Ivy] <i>I need to leave again.</i>

5
00:00:15,682 --> 00:00:18,101
<i>They found a lead on Arthur's whereabouts.</i>

6
00:00:18,184 --> 00:00:21,104
<i>There's a possibility that</i>
<i>Arthur escaped from the drum.</i>

7
00:00:21,187 --> 00:00:22,397
<i>-Mr. Mayor!</i>
<i>-Ivy!</i>

8
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,733
<i>-Ivy!</i>
<i>-Mr. Mayor, she's not here!</i>

9
00:00:24,816 --> 00:00:26,443
[Arnaldo] <i>Then why is her cell phone here?</i>

10
00:00:26,526 --> 00:00:28,403
<i>-She left it behi--</i>
<i>-Liar!</i>

11
00:00:28,486 --> 00:00:29,612
[Carlotta gasps]

12
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:30,488
<i>Ivy!</i>

13
00:00:30,572 --> 00:00:32,323
<i>Ivy, come out here! Open the door!</i>

14
00:00:32,407 --> 00:00:35,577
<i>-Nanny?</i>
<i>-Ivy… Ivy, the…</i>

15
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:37,370
-<i>Nanny?</i>
-[Arnaldo screams]

16
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:38,747
[Carlotta choking]

17
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:40,790
[Ivy] <i>I think something happened</i>
<i>to Nanny Carlotta.</i>

18
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:42,876
<i>Nanny Carlotta?</i>

19
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:46,254
[Ivy screaming and wailing]

20
00:00:46,337 --> 00:00:49,841
<i>Who did this to you?!</i>

21
00:00:49,924 --> 00:00:51,718
[police officer] <i>We can't find</i>
<i>any signs of foul play.</i>

22
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:53,636
<i>It looks like a suicide, Miss Aguas.</i>

23
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,638
<i>Do you know what that murderer did?</i>

24
00:00:55,722 --> 00:00:57,807
<i>They wiped the crime scene clean</i>

25
00:00:57,891 --> 00:00:59,309
<i>to make it look like</i>

26
00:00:59,392 --> 00:01:01,728
<i>Nanny Carlotta committed suicide.</i>

27
00:01:01,811 --> 00:01:04,147
[Julio] <i>What do you know about the death</i>

28
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:05,732
<i>of Ivy Aguas' sweet old nanny?</i>

29
00:01:05,815 --> 00:01:07,108
[Arnaldo] <i>I lost control of my emotions!</i>

30
00:01:07,192 --> 00:01:09,652
<i>I went there because Diego</i>
<i>started making a move on Ivy.</i>

31
00:01:09,736 --> 00:01:13,698
<i>You shouldn't have let</i>
<i>that woman get into your head.</i>

32
00:01:13,782 --> 00:01:15,241
[Diego] <i>Ivy, I know what you're thinking.</i>

33
00:01:15,325 --> 00:01:17,911
<i>You know who's behind</i>
<i>Miss Carlotta's murder.</i>

34
00:01:17,994 --> 00:01:19,079
<i>It was one of the Ardientes.</i>

35
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:22,040
[Ivy] <i>Nanny, help me find</i>

36
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:23,750
<i>the monster who killed you.</i>

37
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:25,710
<i>I'll find out who that person is,</i>

38
00:01:25,794 --> 00:01:27,670
<i>and I'll make them pay.</i>

39
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:29,714
<i>A-A-T.</i>

40
00:01:29,798 --> 00:01:34,260
<i>Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

41
00:01:34,344 --> 00:01:38,556
<i>What do you have to do</i>
<i>with Nanny Carlotta's death?</i>

42
00:01:41,601 --> 00:01:43,686
Where's the other cufflink?

43
00:01:44,145 --> 00:01:45,438
I'm sorry, Mayor,

44
00:01:45,522 --> 00:01:46,689
but I'm afraid there wasn't any--

45
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:49,776
-Just admit you messed up!
-I'm sorry.

46
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:51,027
Get out of my face!

47
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:54,072
If you can't find it,
I'll shove this down your throat!

48
00:01:54,739 --> 00:01:55,740
Now go!

49
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:03,373
Arnaldo.

50
00:02:04,374 --> 00:02:08,086
What's going on? Why are you shouting?

51
00:02:08,169 --> 00:02:09,379
I'm sorry, Grandpa.

52
00:02:09,462 --> 00:02:12,799
The maids lost one
of the cufflinks you gave me.

53
00:02:13,383 --> 00:02:14,801
The one with your initials?

54
00:02:16,636 --> 00:02:17,804
Yes.

55
00:02:17,887 --> 00:02:19,347
Weren't you

56
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:22,350
wearing it yesterday?

57
00:02:23,601 --> 00:02:25,186
Are you sure you didn't leave it

58
00:02:25,270 --> 00:02:27,188
at Ivy Aguas' house?

59
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:29,023
[tense music playing]

60
00:02:29,774 --> 00:02:30,984
No.

61
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:32,402
Impossible.

62
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:34,445
I made sure they wouldn't find
any evidence.

63
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:35,738
Are you sure?

64
00:02:35,822 --> 00:02:37,407
Yes, I'm sure.

65
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:38,616
We cleaned the place up.

66
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:40,326
I made sure, okay?

67
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:43,329
[exhales]

68
00:02:45,665 --> 00:02:48,042
[tense music playing]

69
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:50,003
Ivy.

70
00:02:50,086 --> 00:02:51,337
Arnaldo.

71
00:03:02,223 --> 00:03:03,600
[cries]

72
00:03:03,683 --> 00:03:04,893
Arnaldo.

73
00:03:05,351 --> 00:03:08,271
I heard what happened.
I wanted to see you, but--

74
00:03:11,149 --> 00:03:13,610
[crying]

75
00:03:13,985 --> 00:03:17,322
We Ardientes offer
our condolences, Miss Aguas.

76
00:03:22,535 --> 00:03:23,786
Thank you.

77
00:03:27,248 --> 00:03:28,791
Can you tell me what happened?

78
00:03:31,002 --> 00:03:34,464
Nanny Carlotta called me before she died.

79
00:03:36,799 --> 00:03:38,843
When I came home, it was too late.

80
00:03:39,969 --> 00:03:43,139
I saw her body hanging, Arnaldo.

81
00:03:45,975 --> 00:03:48,019
[stutters] I'm sorry, I wasn't there.

82
00:03:49,771 --> 00:03:52,398
I've been trying to call you.
Where were you?

83
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:54,359
I know.

84
00:03:54,776 --> 00:03:56,152
I'm sorry, I'm here now.

85
00:03:58,655 --> 00:03:59,781
Arnaldo.

86
00:04:01,991 --> 00:04:05,787
[suspenseful music playing]

87
00:04:12,794 --> 00:04:13,795
Sit down, sit down.

88
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:24,931
What happened to your hand?

89
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:27,267
This?

90
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:28,351
Um…

91
00:04:29,352 --> 00:04:31,896
I was blowing off some steam
at the firing range.

92
00:04:32,772 --> 00:04:34,482
It's a stupid mistake.

93
00:04:34,565 --> 00:04:35,817
I cocked the gun the wrong way.

94
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:37,777
Anyway…

95
00:04:38,152 --> 00:04:39,779
I just want to say sorry.

96
00:04:40,905 --> 00:04:43,658
I wasn't there when you needed me.

97
00:04:44,784 --> 00:04:47,912
I was too busy with the campaign.

98
00:04:48,371 --> 00:04:51,082
I didn't realize there was
no reception in the area.

99
00:04:51,165 --> 00:04:52,458
It won't happen again.

100
00:04:52,542 --> 00:04:53,584
I promise.

101
00:05:05,388 --> 00:05:08,349
[tense music swells]

102
00:05:16,607 --> 00:05:17,859
Diego.

103
00:05:17,942 --> 00:05:20,320
Lily's not picking up my calls.

104
00:05:21,195 --> 00:05:23,990
She probably wants to
spend some time alone.

105
00:05:24,073 --> 00:05:24,949
[sighs]

106
00:05:26,367 --> 00:05:28,619
I want to comfort my daughter…

107
00:05:29,203 --> 00:05:30,705
but I can't be with her.

108
00:05:31,622 --> 00:05:34,709
I can't let the Ardientes know
that I'm her mother.

109
00:05:35,793 --> 00:05:37,795
We both feel the same way.

110
00:05:39,756 --> 00:05:41,924
I can't do the things
I want to do for her…

111
00:05:43,801 --> 00:05:46,512
because it might ruin her plans.

112
00:05:48,264 --> 00:05:49,682
Like loving her.

113
00:05:51,809 --> 00:05:53,561
But I'm not giving up.

114
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:55,813
I'll wait for her.

115
00:05:56,314 --> 00:05:58,775
[soft piano music playing]

116
00:06:06,783 --> 00:06:09,243
[tense music playing]

117
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:20,797
Arnaldo.

118
00:06:22,507 --> 00:06:23,800
Take me away.

119
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:26,803
I want to get out of this town.

120
00:06:28,888 --> 00:06:30,807
Yes. I'll do that.

121
00:06:33,309 --> 00:06:35,269
I'll do that. I'll take you away.

122
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:37,105
We'll go somewhere far away.

123
00:06:37,188 --> 00:06:38,981
I'll make you forget everything.

124
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:42,777
Come here.

125
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:01,879
[Arnaldo] Hey, what's wrong?

126
00:07:02,797 --> 00:07:04,048
What's this?

127
00:07:05,216 --> 00:07:06,509
Is this yours?

128
00:07:07,385 --> 00:07:08,302
Yeah, that's mine.

129
00:07:10,054 --> 00:07:11,139
I've been looking for it.

130
00:07:19,772 --> 00:07:22,442
[tense music intensifies]

131
00:07:31,075 --> 00:07:32,702
Lily, why did you do that?

132
00:07:33,369 --> 00:07:36,456
You shouldn't have gone
to the Ardientes' mansion alone.

133
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:37,874
What if you're right,

134
00:07:37,957 --> 00:07:40,793
and they had something to do
with Carlotta's death?

135
00:07:40,877 --> 00:07:42,712
What if they kill you next?

136
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:46,841
Nanny Carlotta was murdered
for a different reason.

137
00:07:48,634 --> 00:07:49,719
Like what?

138
00:07:50,428 --> 00:07:51,596
That's what I'll find out.

139
00:07:53,890 --> 00:07:56,809
After the cremation,
I'll go on a vacation.

140
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:58,978
I'll be gone for a few days.

141
00:07:59,061 --> 00:08:00,646
And where are you going?

142
00:08:01,772 --> 00:08:03,691
I asked Arnaldo to decide.

143
00:08:03,774 --> 00:08:05,193
I'm not sure, either.

144
00:08:06,235 --> 00:08:07,820
You're leaving with Arnaldo?

145
00:08:15,077 --> 00:08:16,704
Okay, I'll be gone for a few days,

146
00:08:16,787 --> 00:08:18,372
but the work here doesn't stop.

147
00:08:18,456 --> 00:08:19,707
In fact, you'll work double time

148
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:21,626
because I want this campaign
running without me.

149
00:08:21,709 --> 00:08:24,712
Mayor, how can we run
the campaign without you?

150
00:08:24,795 --> 00:08:27,298
The voters want to see you.

151
00:08:27,381 --> 00:08:30,801
The last time I checked,
I pay you to think of solutions,

152
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:32,762
and not to give me more problems.

153
00:08:33,137 --> 00:08:34,430
So, do whatever it takes.

154
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:36,349
You can invite celebrities,

155
00:08:36,432 --> 00:08:37,725
hire sexy dancers,

156
00:08:37,808 --> 00:08:42,480
or do any gimmicks
to fill our events with people.

157
00:08:42,563 --> 00:08:45,149
So, I want a clear plan
of action by noon today. Go.

158
00:08:45,691 --> 00:08:46,692
Yes, Mayor.

159
00:08:49,570 --> 00:08:50,988
You know, Arnaldo…

160
00:08:52,448 --> 00:08:56,619
I have a strong feeling that
your obsession with Ivy Aguas…

161
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:00,081
will be the cause of your downfall.

162
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:01,791
Just relax, Grandpa.

163
00:09:01,874 --> 00:09:03,376
Ivy is an inspiration,

164
00:09:03,459 --> 00:09:05,753
and she's the reason
why I'm working so hard.

165
00:09:05,836 --> 00:09:07,255
So, leave her alone.

166
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:12,802
What did she do, for you
to be head over heels for her?

167
00:09:13,177 --> 00:09:16,639
Has she given you the works?

168
00:09:18,099 --> 00:09:19,725
Well, not yet.

169
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:21,811
But we'll get there.

170
00:09:23,646 --> 00:09:26,857
Don't laugh because
I'm not joking with you.

171
00:09:27,775 --> 00:09:28,901
I'm warning you.

172
00:09:29,443 --> 00:09:32,280
Be careful when you're around that woman,

173
00:09:32,363 --> 00:09:34,031
because if she finds out what you did…

174
00:09:35,116 --> 00:09:38,869
then I'll be forced to kill her,
and you know I won't hesitate.

175
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:40,788
Understand?

176
00:09:42,707 --> 00:09:43,708
[sighs]

177
00:09:43,791 --> 00:09:45,793
[tense music intensifies]

178
00:09:46,544 --> 00:09:48,254
[Julio] Here she comes!

179
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:49,797
Arnaldo!

180
00:09:50,798 --> 00:09:52,717
What's this I heard from your staff

181
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:54,051
about you going on a vacation?

182
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:57,179
You know, Emilia,
you arrived at the perfect time.

183
00:09:57,847 --> 00:09:59,849
Talk to your son.

184
00:10:00,391 --> 00:10:02,393
Because you're very similar.

185
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:05,938
You're both fools for love.

186
00:10:06,022 --> 00:10:07,106
[Julio laughs]

187
00:10:07,189 --> 00:10:08,774
Hey, what's going on?

188
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:10,318
[Julio sighs]

189
00:10:12,695 --> 00:10:14,780
Ivy. Ivy, wait.

190
00:10:17,408 --> 00:10:19,368
I know you're only doing this
to get back at them.

191
00:10:20,786 --> 00:10:22,038
But what are you planning to do?

192
00:10:24,206 --> 00:10:25,833
Ivy, why won't you tell me?

193
00:10:26,667 --> 00:10:28,169
Don't you trust me?

194
00:10:28,919 --> 00:10:30,713
This isn't about trust.

195
00:10:31,797 --> 00:10:34,008
It's just better that none of you know.

196
00:10:40,806 --> 00:10:41,807
Diego.

197
00:10:45,144 --> 00:10:47,188
Let's be patient with Lily.

198
00:10:49,774 --> 00:10:51,275
Whatever she's doing…

199
00:10:52,568 --> 00:10:53,819
I know she has her reasons.

200
00:10:55,988 --> 00:10:57,156
[Diego] I understand.

201
00:10:58,783 --> 00:11:02,662
I'm just worried because
what she's doing is dangerous.

202
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:04,121
Diego, I feel the same.

203
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:06,165
I'm worried too.

204
00:11:07,708 --> 00:11:09,877
Even though I know
Lily can handle herself…

205
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:13,714
as her mother, I'm still scared for her.

206
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:17,885
Diego just promise me…

207
00:11:18,969 --> 00:11:20,679
you'll protect my daughter.

208
00:11:22,181 --> 00:11:23,224
I promise.

209
00:11:24,809 --> 00:11:27,603
If only I could stay
by her side all the time,

210
00:11:27,686 --> 00:11:28,771
I would.

211
00:11:29,772 --> 00:11:32,441
But now I have other things
to take care of.

212
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:34,276
Where are you going?

213
00:11:34,902 --> 00:11:36,445
I'm going to look for Arthur.

214
00:11:37,071 --> 00:11:38,531
If he really is alive,

215
00:11:38,614 --> 00:11:40,741
I know the Ardientes are hunting him down.

216
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:43,536
I'll convince him to testify against them.

217
00:11:50,042 --> 00:11:53,212
<i>I'm sorry that I have</i>
<i>to keep secrets from you.</i>

218
00:11:53,295 --> 00:11:56,674
<i>But I have to avenge</i>
<i>Nanny Carlotta's death.</i>

219
00:11:57,258 --> 00:11:59,009
<i>You don't have to be part of this.</i>

220
00:11:59,677 --> 00:12:01,679
<i>I can't let others experience</i>

221
00:12:01,762 --> 00:12:04,056
<i>what happened to Nanny Carlotta and Jepoy.</i>

222
00:12:05,266 --> 00:12:09,061
[Ivy] <i>The Ardientes won't hurt</i>
<i>any of my loved ones again.</i>

223
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:17,153
You will not go with that woman alone.

224
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:19,864
I'm not a child anymore.
I can do whatever I want.

225
00:12:20,781 --> 00:12:22,199
Arnaldo, my son!

226
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:24,160
That woman's got you on a leash.

227
00:12:24,243 --> 00:12:27,663
Who knows? She might just
dupe you into marrying her!

228
00:12:28,789 --> 00:12:30,082
Ivy's different.

229
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:31,292
She's not like you.

230
00:12:31,792 --> 00:12:33,085
Excuse me, Arnaldo,

231
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:34,879
but I didn't trick your father.

232
00:12:35,463 --> 00:12:36,630
Yeah, right.

233
00:12:36,714 --> 00:12:37,715
Listen to me.

234
00:12:37,798 --> 00:12:39,717
I don't like that woman for you.

235
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:41,051
I don't trust her.

236
00:12:41,677 --> 00:12:44,180
Well, you can say whatever you want, okay?

237
00:12:44,263 --> 00:12:46,265
But my feelings for Ivy won't change,

238
00:12:46,807 --> 00:12:48,058
and that's final.

239
00:12:48,809 --> 00:12:49,810
Excuse me.

240
00:13:00,321 --> 00:13:02,948
[ominous music playing]

241
00:13:10,998 --> 00:13:12,041
Mister.

242
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:13,792
Mister, can I ask you something?

243
00:13:17,338 --> 00:13:18,380
Mister.

244
00:13:18,797 --> 00:13:20,799
Good evening. Can I ask you something?

245
00:13:22,301 --> 00:13:23,719
-What is it?
-Uh…

246
00:13:23,802 --> 00:13:25,429
Do you recognize this man?

247
00:13:28,265 --> 00:13:29,767
I think I've seen him.

248
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:30,935
Really?

249
00:13:31,810 --> 00:13:33,395
When did you see him?

250
00:13:33,896 --> 00:13:35,731
I can't remember when,

251
00:13:35,814 --> 00:13:36,982
but I've seen this man.

252
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:38,776
He probably lives around here.

253
00:13:41,487 --> 00:13:43,781
-Thank you.
-No problem.

254
00:13:57,002 --> 00:13:58,462
What did Papa say?

255
00:13:58,546 --> 00:14:00,798
Are we going to Carlotta's wake?

256
00:14:01,298 --> 00:14:03,217
I don't know, and I don't care.

257
00:14:03,842 --> 00:14:06,804
Honestly, I'd rather relax or go to a spa

258
00:14:06,887 --> 00:14:10,140
than go there
to put up with Ivy wailing over

259
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:12,476
the death of her foster mother.

260
00:14:12,810 --> 00:14:14,645
You know, she's just craving attention.

261
00:14:17,064 --> 00:14:20,192
Emilia, I was just asking a question.

262
00:14:20,276 --> 00:14:21,819
Don't stress yourself over it.

263
00:14:22,486 --> 00:14:25,573
How about I just give you a massage?

264
00:14:26,824 --> 00:14:28,826
Wait, Raul. Hold on.

265
00:14:28,909 --> 00:14:31,036
Did you do something wrong again?

266
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,705
Are you cheating on me again?

267
00:14:32,788 --> 00:14:35,082
No! I'm just being a good husband.

268
00:14:35,165 --> 00:14:37,126
A good husband? Why?

269
00:14:37,209 --> 00:14:39,503
Why, is that a big deal?
If you don't like it, then fine!

270
00:14:39,587 --> 00:14:40,713
I'll go back to my old self.

271
00:14:40,796 --> 00:14:42,089
I didn't mean that.

272
00:14:42,172 --> 00:14:43,507
Stop it, you.

273
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:46,051
Okay, how about this, Emilia?

274
00:14:48,304 --> 00:14:49,680
Have dinner with me,

275
00:14:49,763 --> 00:14:52,433
and we'll talk about things
that need to be discussed.

276
00:14:52,516 --> 00:14:56,020
Let's fix everything as husband and wife.

277
00:14:57,605 --> 00:14:58,689
Wait.

278
00:14:58,772 --> 00:15:00,816
Are you asking me out on a date?

279
00:15:01,358 --> 00:15:02,693
I don't know.

280
00:15:02,776 --> 00:15:06,322
But I just want to be with you.

281
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:08,616
Wow.

282
00:15:09,283 --> 00:15:10,576
What's gotten into you?

283
00:15:10,659 --> 00:15:11,911
Nothing.

284
00:15:27,217 --> 00:15:28,260
Arthur.

285
00:15:28,886 --> 00:15:31,639
When do you plan on going to the police?

286
00:15:33,807 --> 00:15:35,726
After everything I've been through

287
00:15:35,809 --> 00:15:37,519
at the hands of the Ardientes?

288
00:15:39,313 --> 00:15:41,148
I don't want to come out of hiding.

289
00:15:41,231 --> 00:15:44,109
What about your fight for justice?

290
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:47,237
There is no justice in Poblacion Ardiente.

291
00:15:48,322 --> 00:15:51,325
They're going to kill anyone
who stands in their way.

292
00:15:51,867 --> 00:15:54,536
I'd rather have them think I'm dead.

293
00:15:54,995 --> 00:15:56,413
I'll do everything…

294
00:15:57,915 --> 00:15:59,708
even if it means I have to kill…

295
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:02,795
just to keep them from
finding out I'm still alive.

296
00:16:10,344 --> 00:16:11,804
This one's strong!

297
00:16:12,805 --> 00:16:14,390
-Hmm?
-Hi.

298
00:16:14,848 --> 00:16:15,849
Hi.

299
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:19,687
Raul Torillo.

300
00:16:20,562 --> 00:16:22,439
-I know.
-Raul Torillo.

301
00:16:22,773 --> 00:16:23,774
-Hi.
-You are?

302
00:16:23,857 --> 00:16:24,900
I'm Emilia.

303
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:26,902
[both laughing]

304
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:28,946
-What are you doing?
-Too cheesy?

305
00:16:29,571 --> 00:16:30,698
Is it just me,

306
00:16:30,781 --> 00:16:32,241
or is there something about tonight?

307
00:16:32,324 --> 00:16:33,492
It's like…

308
00:16:33,575 --> 00:16:35,536
What are you talking about?

309
00:16:36,286 --> 00:16:39,164
-This is how we met.
-[giggles]

310
00:16:39,248 --> 00:16:40,708
-Right?
-Yes, I remember.

311
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:43,460
We'd always have fun like this.

312
00:16:43,544 --> 00:16:44,712
Exactly like this.

313
00:16:44,795 --> 00:16:46,296
I know. That's why we're here.

314
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:47,589
We're having fun, aren't we?

315
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:49,008
Is that why you brought me here?

316
00:16:49,091 --> 00:16:50,718
Yes. Because I wanted us to have fun.

317
00:16:50,801 --> 00:16:52,469
-Okay?
-I see.

318
00:16:52,553 --> 00:16:56,807
How do I know this isn't just for tonight?

319
00:16:58,183 --> 00:16:59,226
Emilia.

320
00:17:02,146 --> 00:17:04,398
I'm sure you feel it too, don't you?

321
00:17:05,315 --> 00:17:06,400
Prove it.

322
00:17:07,192 --> 00:17:09,278
[giggling]

323
00:17:09,361 --> 00:17:11,155
I'm serious, okay?

324
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:12,239
Okay.

325
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:14,658
I want you back.

326
00:17:16,326 --> 00:17:18,078
I want things back the way they were.

327
00:17:19,788 --> 00:17:21,790
I want us to be happy.

328
00:17:23,375 --> 00:17:25,252
Not a problem in the world.

329
00:17:25,335 --> 00:17:27,504
Although, we do have a few now.

330
00:17:27,588 --> 00:17:29,965
But we'll just laugh them off.

331
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:33,343
Or, better yet,
we can just stay in our room.

332
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:36,513
-Right?
-[both giggle]

333
00:17:37,639 --> 00:17:39,725
No, I'm serious. I really am.

334
00:17:42,144 --> 00:17:44,104
If you want me to court you, I'll do it.

335
00:17:44,813 --> 00:17:46,273
-Really?
-I will.

336
00:17:51,779 --> 00:17:53,781
[giggling]

337
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:56,033
[Emilia giggles]

338
00:17:56,116 --> 00:17:58,619
-What? Okay.
-People are watching.

339
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:00,746
You love me, right?

340
00:18:00,829 --> 00:18:02,790
-Of course, you do.
-Should I say yes now?

341
00:18:02,873 --> 00:18:04,792
You don't have to answer that.
Just kiss me.

342
00:18:05,626 --> 00:18:07,336
Just kiss me then, that's it.

343
00:18:07,419 --> 00:18:08,545
I'm good with that.

344
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:17,304
<i>Oh, my goodness. It's actually working.</i>

345
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:20,474
<i>She's so desperate.</i>

346
00:18:24,061 --> 00:18:28,607
<i>This is the beginning</i>
<i>of your downfall, Emilia.</i>

347
00:18:31,318 --> 00:18:34,321
[Raul and Emilia laugh]

348
00:18:39,785 --> 00:18:42,788
[ominous music playing]

349
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:57,344
She's in a better place now.

350
00:19:01,807 --> 00:19:02,808
[cries]

351
00:19:14,903 --> 00:19:18,615
Why did this have to happen, Arnaldo?

352
00:19:26,206 --> 00:19:29,626
I wish I could dream of Nanny Carlotta.

353
00:19:30,794 --> 00:19:32,796
So she could tell me…

354
00:19:33,797 --> 00:19:36,216
who did this to her.

355
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:39,636
[tense music playing]

356
00:19:42,806 --> 00:19:45,517
[fakes crying]

357
00:20:04,995 --> 00:20:07,623
[phone ringing]

358
00:20:11,668 --> 00:20:12,711
[Camia] <i>Diego?</i>

359
00:20:12,794 --> 00:20:13,837
Aunt Camia.

360
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:15,714
Someone spotted Arthur.

361
00:20:16,340 --> 00:20:18,050
[Diego] <i>I'll keep going back there until…</i>

362
00:20:18,133 --> 00:20:19,259
I find him.

363
00:20:19,343 --> 00:20:20,594
[Camia] <i>Diego, just be careful, okay?</i>

364
00:20:20,677 --> 00:20:23,347
The Ardientes can't
find out he's still alive.

365
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:24,723
Yes, Aunt Camia.

366
00:20:24,806 --> 00:20:25,724
I have to go now.

367
00:20:25,807 --> 00:20:26,975
Take care, Diego.

368
00:20:36,443 --> 00:20:38,195
[car engine turns over]

369
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:46,119
Nanny, make this the centerpiece, okay?

370
00:20:47,621 --> 00:20:49,623
Clean this later.

371
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:51,959
So beautiful. [giggles]

372
00:20:53,126 --> 00:20:54,294
Hi, Auntie.

373
00:20:54,378 --> 00:20:55,629
You're blooming.

374
00:20:58,131 --> 00:21:00,717
-Did you have fun last night?
-[laughs]

375
00:21:00,801 --> 00:21:02,219
You're so naughty, Aunt Claire.

376
00:21:02,302 --> 00:21:03,929
Well, that smile of yours

377
00:21:04,012 --> 00:21:05,847
reminds me of a giggling teenager.

378
00:21:06,807 --> 00:21:09,184
Well, that's what love can do, Auntie.

379
00:21:09,268 --> 00:21:10,811
It makes you feel young again.

380
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:13,021
So, you're in love?

381
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:14,982
At last!

382
00:21:15,774 --> 00:21:17,776
You finally called it quits with Raul.

383
00:21:18,443 --> 00:21:20,779
So, tell me, who's the lucky guy?

384
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:24,283
Auntie, there's no new guy.
It's still the same.

385
00:21:24,366 --> 00:21:26,868
I still love Raul.
From then on and forever,

386
00:21:26,952 --> 00:21:28,578
he will always be the love of my life.

387
00:21:28,662 --> 00:21:30,747
Raul is like wine.

388
00:21:30,831 --> 00:21:33,125
The longer it's aged, the better it gets.

389
00:21:33,792 --> 00:21:35,002
Disgusting.

390
00:21:35,794 --> 00:21:38,338
When will you stop believing Raul's lies?

391
00:21:38,797 --> 00:21:41,717
Auntie, we talked over dinner last night.

392
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:44,761
He told me he would court me again,

393
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:47,514
that he'd change,
that he loves me very much.

394
00:21:47,597 --> 00:21:48,932
I already heard that.

395
00:21:49,016 --> 00:21:50,809
Your husband is cunning.

396
00:21:50,892 --> 00:21:52,102
So if I were you,

397
00:21:52,185 --> 00:21:56,690
test him first before
believing anything he says.

398
00:21:56,773 --> 00:21:58,483
Auntie, you're so pessimistic.

399
00:21:58,567 --> 00:22:00,110
You became an old maid

400
00:22:00,193 --> 00:22:02,029
because you always think like that.

401
00:22:02,112 --> 00:22:04,781
You know, if there's one thing
I learned about love…

402
00:22:05,657 --> 00:22:07,409
Nothing is impossible with love.

403
00:22:09,703 --> 00:22:11,913
You know why I didn't get married?

404
00:22:12,581 --> 00:22:15,083
Because all men are liars.

405
00:22:15,584 --> 00:22:17,878
And your husband is no exception.

406
00:22:17,961 --> 00:22:19,713
Auntie, you're such a man-hater.

407
00:22:19,796 --> 00:22:21,798
Now I'm curious who turned you into one.

408
00:22:21,882 --> 00:22:22,924
Why so bitter?

409
00:22:32,059 --> 00:22:33,852
Just give me more time.

410
00:22:33,935 --> 00:22:35,145
Okay, Natalie?

411
00:22:39,775 --> 00:22:40,776
Okay.

412
00:22:41,777 --> 00:22:43,528
But I've just realized,

413
00:22:44,071 --> 00:22:45,739
you really are a bastard.

414
00:22:46,448 --> 00:22:47,949
I actually love it.

415
00:22:48,742 --> 00:22:51,244
-Really? I'm a bastard?
-Mm-hm.

416
00:22:51,328 --> 00:22:53,455
-Yes, you are.
-Okay.

417
00:22:53,538 --> 00:22:56,583
[both giggle]

418
00:22:56,666 --> 00:22:57,959
-Am I a bastard?
-Yeah!

419
00:22:58,043 --> 00:23:00,045
[Raul laughs]

420
00:23:00,128 --> 00:23:02,339
Excuse me. Good evening.

421
00:23:02,422 --> 00:23:03,924
-What is it?
-Can I ask you a question?

422
00:23:04,549 --> 00:23:06,593
Do you recognize this man?

423
00:23:07,803 --> 00:23:09,638
I haven't seen this guy around.

424
00:23:09,721 --> 00:23:11,264
Maybe he's from another village.

425
00:23:12,099 --> 00:23:13,517
Okay, thank you.

426
00:23:14,643 --> 00:23:15,852
[woman whispers] We should hurry.

427
00:23:22,692 --> 00:23:24,194
Are you okay, ma'am?

428
00:23:24,778 --> 00:23:26,071
Let me help you.

429
00:23:26,154 --> 00:23:27,197
Thank you.

430
00:23:27,989 --> 00:23:29,699
Your basket is broken.

431
00:23:29,783 --> 00:23:32,369
-You aren't from here, are you?
-I'm not.

432
00:23:32,452 --> 00:23:34,079
I can tell.

433
00:23:34,162 --> 00:23:35,997
I'm looking for someone.

434
00:23:36,540 --> 00:23:37,999
Maybe you recognize this man.

435
00:23:39,918 --> 00:23:41,753
[tense music playing]

436
00:23:41,837 --> 00:23:43,630
Have you seen him before?

437
00:23:47,175 --> 00:23:50,053
No, I haven't. I don't know him.

438
00:23:51,429 --> 00:23:53,723
I'm going now. Please give me that.

439
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:57,811
[tense music intensifies]

440
00:24:06,778 --> 00:24:08,780
Arthur! Arthur!

441
00:24:09,489 --> 00:24:10,240
-Yes?
-Arthur!

442
00:24:10,323 --> 00:24:13,451
You have to leave!
Somebody's looking for you.

443
00:24:13,535 --> 00:24:14,703
Who is it?

444
00:24:14,786 --> 00:24:16,163
I don't know, but maybe…

445
00:24:16,246 --> 00:24:18,290
he's one of the men who wanted you dead.

446
00:24:19,791 --> 00:24:20,709
Hurry!

447
00:24:21,793 --> 00:24:23,170
He might find you here.

448
00:24:31,803 --> 00:24:32,929
Arthur!

449
00:24:35,140 --> 00:24:36,183
Diego?

450
00:24:36,808 --> 00:24:38,268
We need to talk.

451
00:24:40,729 --> 00:24:42,439
Arthur, wait!

452
00:24:42,772 --> 00:24:44,107
Listen, Arthur!

453
00:24:44,191 --> 00:24:46,067
I won't testify against the Ardientes!

454
00:24:50,780 --> 00:24:52,782
Arthur, hear me out first.

455
00:24:52,866 --> 00:24:53,909
Please. Arthur.

456
00:24:56,036 --> 00:24:57,829
Please listen to me?

457
00:25:04,336 --> 00:25:05,837
You shouldn't have looked for me.

458
00:25:08,298 --> 00:25:09,799
Mister Arthur, wait.

459
00:25:11,801 --> 00:25:13,303
I won't put you in danger.

460
00:25:16,056 --> 00:25:18,475
I'll make sure we have
enough evidence in court…

461
00:25:19,267 --> 00:25:20,560
before you give your testimony.

462
00:25:21,728 --> 00:25:22,771
I'm living a quiet life!

463
00:25:23,980 --> 00:25:25,357
You can't ruin it!

464
00:25:26,441 --> 00:25:28,777
Arthur, you can't hide forever.

465
00:25:30,237 --> 00:25:33,531
If I found you, the Ardientes
will find you too!

466
00:25:39,204 --> 00:25:41,623
Arthur, you need us.

467
00:25:42,916 --> 00:25:44,125
We'll help you!

468
00:25:46,795 --> 00:25:48,255
I know you're a good person.

469
00:25:49,631 --> 00:25:51,007
You're not capable of murder.

470
00:25:51,800 --> 00:25:55,053
[tense music intensifies]

471
00:25:59,474 --> 00:26:00,725
Arthur.

472
00:26:00,809 --> 00:26:02,310
Arthur, let's talk.

473
00:26:03,937 --> 00:26:05,105
I'll help you.

474
00:26:06,273 --> 00:26:07,565
We'll help you.

475
00:26:10,235 --> 00:26:11,987
[tense music continues playing]

476
00:26:13,488 --> 00:26:14,489
[cries]

477
00:26:29,254 --> 00:26:30,380
Arthur.

478
00:26:31,214 --> 00:26:32,424
Put the gun down.

479
00:26:44,853 --> 00:26:46,062
Arthur.

480
00:27:07,334 --> 00:27:09,127
I'm going to take Ivy to our resort.

481
00:27:09,210 --> 00:27:11,629
So, if you need me,
you know where to find me.

482
00:27:12,005 --> 00:27:13,256
But…

483
00:27:13,757 --> 00:27:17,093
I hope I don't see you
the whole time I'm with her.

484
00:27:18,345 --> 00:27:20,847
Arnaldo, what's wrong with you?

485
00:27:20,930 --> 00:27:23,433
First, it was Natalie. Now it's Ivy!

486
00:27:23,808 --> 00:27:26,269
Your taste in women is getting worse!

487
00:27:26,686 --> 00:27:27,771
[Julio] You know…

488
00:27:28,646 --> 00:27:31,649
they say that men

489
00:27:31,733 --> 00:27:35,111
fall in love with women who
are similar to their mothers.

490
00:27:36,071 --> 00:27:39,366
Therefore, parents are to blame

491
00:27:39,449 --> 00:27:41,242
for their children's mistakes.

492
00:27:41,326 --> 00:27:44,496
That is why I can never forgive myself

493
00:27:44,996 --> 00:27:46,790
for what happened to you.

494
00:27:48,666 --> 00:27:50,877
Papa, please, can you just help me out?

495
00:27:50,960 --> 00:27:54,255
Let's convince Arnaldo
not to go on this trip with Ivy!

496
00:27:54,339 --> 00:27:55,799
-I'll convince him.
-Go on.

497
00:27:55,882 --> 00:27:57,926
What are you doing, Papa?! Wait!

498
00:27:58,009 --> 00:28:00,720
You mean to tell me not
even a bullet in his head

499
00:28:00,804 --> 00:28:03,515
is going to convince him
to change his mind?!

500
00:28:04,808 --> 00:28:06,518
[laughs]

501
00:28:07,435 --> 00:28:09,771
My dear grandson, Arnaldo.

502
00:28:10,939 --> 00:28:13,983
I asked you to romance Ivy

503
00:28:14,067 --> 00:28:16,694
so we could take her money.

504
00:28:16,778 --> 00:28:19,322
Now, getting her to bed
is just a bonus for you.

505
00:28:19,406 --> 00:28:20,698
That's for your ego.

506
00:28:20,782 --> 00:28:22,325
I can't understand you.

507
00:28:22,409 --> 00:28:25,995
You're handsome, you're rich,
and you're a mayor!

508
00:28:26,079 --> 00:28:27,831
But when it comes to Ivy,

509
00:28:27,914 --> 00:28:29,999
she's got you eating
from the palm of her hand!

510
00:28:30,083 --> 00:28:32,127
You're like a hound dog
being led to slaughter.

511
00:28:32,210 --> 00:28:33,711
Every time Ivy comes up…

512
00:28:33,795 --> 00:28:35,797
[mimics whining dog]

513
00:28:36,798 --> 00:28:38,717
Am I right? You think that's funny?!

514
00:28:38,800 --> 00:28:40,009
It's not funny!

515
00:28:40,093 --> 00:28:42,804
Remember, from time immemorial,
Adam and Eve.

516
00:28:42,887 --> 00:28:46,766
It was Eve who was seduced
and fooled by the snake.

517
00:28:46,850 --> 00:28:49,811
But at this rate, you're going
to get bitten by the snake!

518
00:28:52,063 --> 00:28:53,648
I can't understand you!

519
00:28:59,195 --> 00:29:01,614
Well, I think he's
pushing through with it.

520
00:29:04,492 --> 00:29:06,703
I just hope this time you get the cherry!

521
00:29:07,871 --> 00:29:11,750
[suspenseful music playing]

522
00:29:49,245 --> 00:29:52,791
[sinister music playing]

523
00:30:21,444 --> 00:30:22,946
Mr. Mayor, I want you to choose

524
00:30:23,029 --> 00:30:26,032
which one of these
I should use to kill you.

525
00:30:37,168 --> 00:30:40,630
[sinister music intensifies]

526
00:31:07,740 --> 00:31:09,742
[phone rings]

527
00:31:11,786 --> 00:31:12,787
Mom?

528
00:31:15,790 --> 00:31:17,625
I've already packed my stuff,

529
00:31:17,709 --> 00:31:20,920
including the important things.

530
00:31:22,630 --> 00:31:25,717
My staff are preparing the house
I'll move into.

531
00:31:25,800 --> 00:31:29,596
After my trip, I'll head there right away.

532
00:31:31,139 --> 00:31:32,390
Yes, I'll be careful.

533
00:31:32,473 --> 00:31:33,725
Thank you, Mom.

534
00:31:39,063 --> 00:31:41,774
<i>I promise you, Nanny Carlotta.</i>

535
00:31:42,692 --> 00:31:44,777
<i>I'll make sure…</i>

536
00:31:45,153 --> 00:31:49,365
<i>I make Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo pay.</i>

537
00:32:35,370 --> 00:32:36,788
You're really funny.

538
00:32:39,791 --> 00:32:42,251
Well, anyway, just enjoy the beach,

539
00:32:42,335 --> 00:32:45,046
and make sure nothing bad
happens to Arnaldo.

540
00:32:46,255 --> 00:32:47,173
You know what?

541
00:32:47,256 --> 00:32:50,593
I think you should
stay there alone for good.

542
00:32:51,803 --> 00:32:53,805
If you're envious, then just join us.

543
00:32:54,806 --> 00:32:56,391
No, thanks.

544
00:32:56,808 --> 00:32:58,601
I don't want you to drown me there.

545
00:33:02,814 --> 00:33:04,273
Impressive.

546
00:33:04,983 --> 00:33:07,819
You read my mind.

547
00:33:07,902 --> 00:33:08,987
What about you?

548
00:33:09,070 --> 00:33:10,822
Do you have any idea what I'm thinking?

549
00:33:11,489 --> 00:33:12,699
I'm not interested.

550
00:33:13,366 --> 00:33:18,121
Well, I know you're only using Arnaldo

551
00:33:18,204 --> 00:33:20,206
to get close to our family.

552
00:33:20,707 --> 00:33:22,291
But let me just warn you.

553
00:33:22,375 --> 00:33:24,627
You're messing with the wrong family.

554
00:33:25,753 --> 00:33:27,588
You really love your family, don't you?

555
00:33:27,672 --> 00:33:28,798
I do.

556
00:33:29,590 --> 00:33:30,842
You're like a mother hen.

557
00:33:31,634 --> 00:33:32,802
Sad to say,

558
00:33:33,594 --> 00:33:35,263
they don't like you.

559
00:33:36,806 --> 00:33:38,933
[laughs]

560
00:33:41,227 --> 00:33:43,688
You're testing my patience.

561
00:33:43,771 --> 00:33:44,939
Emilia.

562
00:33:45,982 --> 00:33:47,233
What's wrong?

563
00:33:47,775 --> 00:33:49,068
That's enough.

564
00:33:51,779 --> 00:33:53,031
So…

565
00:33:54,115 --> 00:33:55,783
you two are getting along now.

566
00:33:56,325 --> 00:33:59,495
Why are you so cranky,
if you're happy now?

567
00:34:01,372 --> 00:34:03,875
You're making me envious. Where's Arnaldo?

568
00:34:07,378 --> 00:34:10,089
Arthur has agreed to testify for us again.

569
00:34:10,923 --> 00:34:12,717
To ensure his safety,

570
00:34:12,800 --> 00:34:15,762
we have to make sure
we have enough evidence

571
00:34:15,845 --> 00:34:17,388
before he presents himself in court.

572
00:34:18,473 --> 00:34:19,724
That's good to hear.

573
00:34:20,558 --> 00:34:22,810
Where's Ivy?

574
00:34:23,644 --> 00:34:25,021
Hasn't she told you?

575
00:34:26,606 --> 00:34:28,566
She's leaving with Arnaldo today.

576
00:34:32,904 --> 00:34:35,114
Miss Aguas, the mayor's here.

577
00:34:35,782 --> 00:34:37,241
Arnaldo.

578
00:34:37,950 --> 00:34:38,951
Ivy.

579
00:34:39,619 --> 00:34:41,204
I've been waiting for you.

580
00:34:41,662 --> 00:34:44,707
I'm sorry, I'm late.
The conference just finished.

581
00:34:44,791 --> 00:34:46,292
-But we can go now.
-It's okay.

582
00:34:46,375 --> 00:34:48,169
-Shall we?
-Okay.

583
00:34:51,798 --> 00:34:54,509
Diego, I need your help.

584
00:34:54,592 --> 00:34:56,052
Please follow them.

585
00:34:56,886 --> 00:34:58,387
And watch over my daughter.

586
00:35:00,932 --> 00:35:02,850
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

587
00:35:04,143 --> 00:35:05,686
All right. Bye.

588
00:35:05,770 --> 00:35:07,605
-Shouldn't we see them out?
-Bye, Emilia.

589
00:35:10,441 --> 00:35:11,442
[Emilia] Good grief.

590
00:35:11,526 --> 00:35:14,028
That Arnaldo still hasn't
learned his lesson.

591
00:35:14,487 --> 00:35:15,780
Relax, Emilia.

592
00:35:16,781 --> 00:35:18,991
Our son is an adult.
He knows what he's doing.

593
00:35:19,075 --> 00:35:21,702
But he is falling for the wrong girl.

594
00:35:21,786 --> 00:35:23,663
Why Ivy, of all people?

595
00:35:23,746 --> 00:35:25,915
Of all the women in the world, why her?

596
00:35:25,998 --> 00:35:29,377
We can't tell our son who to love.

597
00:35:29,460 --> 00:35:33,089
But as his parents,
we just have to support him.

598
00:35:33,172 --> 00:35:36,801
Wait, are we actually
discussing this as parents?

599
00:35:36,884 --> 00:35:39,720
Because this is the first time
we've done this.

600
00:35:39,804 --> 00:35:43,182
And I hope this won't be
the last to save our marriage.

601
00:35:43,266 --> 00:35:45,184
We need to fix our family.

602
00:35:45,268 --> 00:35:47,687
Especially my relationship with Arnaldo.

603
00:35:47,770 --> 00:35:49,564
Emilia, to be a better husband,

604
00:35:49,647 --> 00:35:51,149
I have to be a good father.

605
00:35:59,198 --> 00:36:02,326
[phone ringing]

606
00:36:12,712 --> 00:36:13,713
What do you want?

607
00:36:13,796 --> 00:36:15,715
Hello, Diego.

608
00:36:15,798 --> 00:36:17,216
I hope you remember me…

609
00:36:17,675 --> 00:36:18,843
your former mom.

610
00:36:19,385 --> 00:36:22,680
[Emilia] <i>I hope you didn't</i>
<i>delete my number.</i>

611
00:36:22,763 --> 00:36:24,515
I don't have the time to talk to you.

612
00:36:24,599 --> 00:36:27,852
Ivy and Arnaldo are going on a vacation.

613
00:36:27,935 --> 00:36:31,647
Now, do you have the time to talk?

614
00:36:33,024 --> 00:36:34,984
What makes you think I'm interested?

615
00:36:35,526 --> 00:36:37,695
Come on, Diego. I know you.

616
00:36:37,778 --> 00:36:39,071
We're the same.

617
00:36:39,155 --> 00:36:40,656
When we love, we go all in.

618
00:36:41,157 --> 00:36:42,366
<i>You know I'm right.</i>

619
00:36:42,867 --> 00:36:47,413
I'm sure you won't let Arnaldo
have Ivy to himself, right?

620
00:36:48,497 --> 00:36:49,707
Where are they going?

621
00:36:49,790 --> 00:36:52,585
<i>To our beach resort in La Union.</i>

622
00:36:52,668 --> 00:36:53,711
I think you've been there…

623
00:36:53,794 --> 00:36:56,631
when you were still an Ardiente.

624
00:36:57,924 --> 00:37:00,551
But I have a favor to ask.

625
00:37:00,635 --> 00:37:04,764
I hope it doesn't get out that
I gave you this information.

626
00:37:04,847 --> 00:37:08,851
Because even at gunpoint,
I will never admit to it.

627
00:37:08,935 --> 00:37:10,853
Why should I trust you?

628
00:37:10,937 --> 00:37:13,147
Because I don't want my son

629
00:37:13,898 --> 00:37:16,567
to end up with that bitch.

630
00:37:16,651 --> 00:37:19,695
I just know she's better off with you.

631
00:37:19,779 --> 00:37:22,531
So, what are you waiting for?

632
00:37:22,615 --> 00:37:23,991
Go get your girl.

633
00:37:24,533 --> 00:37:25,618
Hurry.

634
00:37:37,004 --> 00:37:41,217
[upbeat music playing]

635
00:38:27,305 --> 00:38:28,389
Do you like it?

636
00:38:30,349 --> 00:38:31,767
[Ivy giggles]

637
00:38:32,893 --> 00:38:34,437
Do you really have to ask?

638
00:38:35,229 --> 00:38:36,314
Of course, I do.

639
00:38:36,981 --> 00:38:38,774
Thanks for bringing me here.

640
00:38:39,734 --> 00:38:40,818
Good.

641
00:38:42,903 --> 00:38:44,947
No one can disturb us here.

642
00:38:45,823 --> 00:38:48,576
It's just you, me…

643
00:38:50,119 --> 00:38:51,620
and this paradise.

644
00:38:57,585 --> 00:38:58,669
Perfect.

645
00:39:20,775 --> 00:39:22,193
What's this?

646
00:39:22,276 --> 00:39:24,362
Diego, where are you going?

647
00:39:25,279 --> 00:39:27,323
I'll be going out for a bit, Nanny.

648
00:39:27,990 --> 00:39:29,283
But I've told the group

649
00:39:29,367 --> 00:39:31,702
what to do with the campaign
while I'm gone.

650
00:39:31,786 --> 00:39:33,079
Where are you going, son?

651
00:39:34,789 --> 00:39:36,707
I'll follow Ivy and Arnaldo.

652
00:39:36,791 --> 00:39:40,086
I need to protect Ivy
because I don't trust Arnaldo.

653
00:39:40,795 --> 00:39:42,505
But, Diego, what if--

654
00:39:42,588 --> 00:39:45,007
Nanny, let me do this.

655
00:39:46,801 --> 00:39:48,386
Nothing bad will happen to me.

656
00:39:51,263 --> 00:39:53,682
All right. Do what you have to do.

657
00:39:53,766 --> 00:39:55,184
Just be careful, okay?

658
00:39:56,143 --> 00:39:57,353
Don't worry about me.

659
00:39:58,187 --> 00:39:59,688
I can take care of myself.

660
00:40:03,818 --> 00:40:04,944
I'm going now, Nanny.

661
00:40:05,778 --> 00:40:06,695
-Uncle.
-Be safe.

662
00:40:06,779 --> 00:40:08,447
-Just take care.
-I will.

663
00:40:08,531 --> 00:40:09,573
Thank you!

664
00:40:15,121 --> 00:40:16,247
Good morning, sir. Good morning, ma'am.

665
00:40:16,330 --> 00:40:17,373
Good morning.

666
00:40:17,832 --> 00:40:20,084
[Arnaldo] I'll just check in here.

667
00:40:20,167 --> 00:40:22,169
-Is our room ready?
-[woman] Yes, sir.

668
00:40:22,253 --> 00:40:24,797
[suspenseful music playing]

669
00:40:30,553 --> 00:40:31,554
Okay, good.

670
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:36,058
[metal detector beeps]

671
00:40:36,809 --> 00:40:39,770
Ma'am, can we open your luggage?

672
00:40:41,105 --> 00:40:42,148
Why?

673
00:40:42,773 --> 00:40:43,941
For inspection, ma'am.

674
00:40:46,902 --> 00:40:48,195
Is there a problem?

675
00:40:51,824 --> 00:40:53,117
And you are?

676
00:40:53,784 --> 00:40:55,703
Special Police Officer 3 Umali,
Congressman.

677
00:40:55,786 --> 00:40:57,580
I'm one of the investigating officers

678
00:40:57,663 --> 00:41:00,124
assigned to Carlotta Naig's suicide case.

679
00:41:00,207 --> 00:41:01,750
Mayor Arnaldo ordered me

680
00:41:01,834 --> 00:41:04,462
to make sure the crime scene
was cleaned up.

681
00:41:05,796 --> 00:41:07,006
Good job, Umali.

682
00:41:07,089 --> 00:41:09,175
They didn't find any evidence.

683
00:41:09,550 --> 00:41:10,801
Thank you, Congressman.

684
00:41:11,510 --> 00:41:12,803
What brings you here?

685
00:41:14,388 --> 00:41:16,724
Do you need your bonus now?

686
00:41:16,807 --> 00:41:17,892
No, Congressman.

687
00:41:17,975 --> 00:41:19,768
I came here to warn the mayor.

688
00:41:20,644 --> 00:41:24,064
The police didn't find any
evidence leading to foul play.

689
00:41:24,148 --> 00:41:26,066
But, Congressman, no matter what we do,

690
00:41:26,150 --> 00:41:27,776
Ivy won't change her mind.

691
00:41:27,860 --> 00:41:31,238
Ivy is convinced
that her nanny was murdered.

692
00:41:31,322 --> 00:41:34,492
She's determined to catch and punish

693
00:41:34,575 --> 00:41:36,160
whoever murdered Carlotta.

694
00:41:37,244 --> 00:41:38,704
So, Congressman,

695
00:41:38,787 --> 00:41:43,834
if Miss Aguas invited the mayor
to go somewhere

696
00:41:43,918 --> 00:41:45,586
she can have him to herself,

697
00:41:45,669 --> 00:41:47,546
he should be careful.

698
00:41:47,630 --> 00:41:49,924
Miss Aguas might be planning
something against him.

699
00:41:51,800 --> 00:41:53,427
Thank you, Umali.

700
00:41:54,094 --> 00:41:56,764
That's very sound advice
that you just gave me.

701
00:41:56,847 --> 00:41:59,183
Anything for you, Congressman.
I'll be on my way.

702
00:41:59,433 --> 00:42:00,935
-Okay.
-Excuse me.

703
00:42:04,772 --> 00:42:06,690
Well, I don't have any problem with that.

704
00:42:06,774 --> 00:42:08,442
But it'll be such a hassle.

705
00:42:08,526 --> 00:42:10,402
Do you really have to do that?

706
00:42:12,780 --> 00:42:15,699
You don't need to check her
things because she's my visitor.

707
00:42:15,783 --> 00:42:17,993
I'm Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo,

708
00:42:18,077 --> 00:42:19,286
and my family owns this place.

709
00:42:19,370 --> 00:42:20,454
Get her things now.

710
00:42:20,538 --> 00:42:22,790
I'm sorry, sir. Sheryl will assist you.

711
00:42:23,791 --> 00:42:25,668
Arnaldo, thank you.

712
00:42:25,751 --> 00:42:26,877
Let's go.

713
00:42:39,723 --> 00:42:40,891
-Please, have a drink.
-Welcome.

714
00:42:40,975 --> 00:42:42,184
Thank you.

715
00:42:43,769 --> 00:42:44,770
Thank you, Mayor.

716
00:42:47,690 --> 00:42:48,857
Okay.

717
00:42:48,941 --> 00:42:50,609
Ivy, this is your room.

718
00:42:56,156 --> 00:42:58,701
I'll just be in the next one.

719
00:42:58,784 --> 00:43:00,786
So you can call me any time.

720
00:43:01,829 --> 00:43:02,871
Thank you.

721
00:43:04,748 --> 00:43:06,959
You know, this place is quiet at night.

722
00:43:09,670 --> 00:43:10,796
It gets lonely.

723
00:43:16,302 --> 00:43:17,720
So?

724
00:43:18,804 --> 00:43:19,805
So…

725
00:43:21,807 --> 00:43:23,517
I'm suggesting

726
00:43:24,602 --> 00:43:25,686
we share a room.

727
00:43:25,769 --> 00:43:27,021
It would be more fun.

728
00:43:33,277 --> 00:43:34,695
[Ivy giggles]

729
00:43:36,614 --> 00:43:39,700
Arnaldo, you're always excited.

730
00:43:39,783 --> 00:43:40,701
Can you blame me?

731
00:43:40,784 --> 00:43:42,953
I just want to make
the most out of this trip.

732
00:43:46,790 --> 00:43:48,834
It pays to be patient, Arnaldo.

733
00:43:49,460 --> 00:43:51,170
It pays to be patient.

734
00:43:55,966 --> 00:43:57,676
Why are you playing hard to get?

735
00:43:59,386 --> 00:44:01,055
Just don't give up.

736
00:44:01,805 --> 00:44:05,142
I promise you, all your effort

737
00:44:05,809 --> 00:44:07,811
and all the time you've waited…

738
00:44:09,772 --> 00:44:11,023
It will be worth it.

739
00:44:12,775 --> 00:44:14,026
Promise.

740
00:44:14,693 --> 00:44:17,780
[tense music playing]

741
00:44:53,524 --> 00:44:54,817
[Julio] <i>Who's that from?</i>

742
00:44:54,900 --> 00:44:56,360
<i>It's from a certain Jaguar.</i>

743
00:44:56,443 --> 00:44:59,655
<i>Jaguar? I've never heard that name before.</i>

744
00:44:59,738 --> 00:45:03,033
<i>This newcomer has some nerve.</i>

745
00:45:07,830 --> 00:45:09,498
[Ivy] <i>Why are you here?</i>

746
00:45:09,581 --> 00:45:10,833
[Diego] <i>I'm here to watch over you.</i>

747
00:45:10,916 --> 00:45:12,668
<i>I don't trust Arnaldo.</i>

748
00:45:12,751 --> 00:45:14,628
<i>You'll ruin my plans.</i>

749
00:45:14,711 --> 00:45:16,046
<i>What do you want me to do?</i>

750
00:45:16,130 --> 00:45:17,256
<i>Kneel before me.</i>

751
00:45:17,339 --> 00:45:18,674
<i>Kiss my feet.</i>

752
00:45:18,757 --> 00:45:19,967
<i>Worship me.</i>

753
00:45:21,260 --> 00:45:23,387
<i>Don't worry about Arnaldo.</i>

754
00:45:23,470 --> 00:45:25,472
<i>I can protect myself.</i>

755
00:45:25,556 --> 00:45:29,184
[theme music playing]
